.TH X2089 6 "October 2026" "2089 0.1.0" "Games"
.SH NAME
x2089 \- the game of 2048, for the X Window System
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B x2089
[
.B \-display
.I host:n
] [
.B \-geometry
.I WxH+X+Y
] [
.B \-fn
.I font
] [
.B \-mono
] [
.B \-u
] [
.B \-s
.I size
] [
.B \-r
.I seed
] [
.B \-l
.I savestring
]
.br
.B x2089
.B \-v
|
.B \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B x2089
is the game of 2048 in a window of its own, drawn with nothing but
Xlib, so it runs wherever X11 does.
The rules are those of
.BR 2089 (6):
slide the tiles, join equal ones, and reach 2048 to win, then keep going
if you like until no move is left.
.PP
The window can be resized, and the board follows, its numbers in the
largest bitmap Helvetica Bold the server has that fits.
The tiles from 2 to 2048 are in the original game's colors; past 2048
they go from green to blue to violet, as many of those as the
colormap has room for (the rest in the original's one dark color).
On a monochrome or grayscale display, or one whose colormap is full,
the board is black and white, tiles going from outlined to reverse
video as they grow.
.B c
switches between the two.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-display " host:n"
The X display to use; the default is
.BR $DISPLAY .
.TP
.BI \-geometry " WxH+X+Y"
The window's size and place.
.TP
.BI \-fn " font"
The font for the score and messages
.RB ( \-font
too).
.TP
.B \-mono
Black and white, even on a color display.
.TP
.B \-u
Allow undo.
.TP
.BI \-s " size"
A board
.I size
cells across, from 2 to 8.
The default is 4.
.TP
.BI \-r " seed"
Play game number
.IR seed ,
from 0 to 4294967295: the same number and size always deal the same
game.
.TP
.BI \-l " savestring"
Carry on a saved game.
.TP
.B \-v
Print the version.
.TP
.B \-h
Print a summary of the options.
.SH KEYS
Type in the window.
.TP
.BR "w a s d" , " k h j l" , " 8 4 2 6" ", or the arrow keys"
Move up, left, down or right.
.TP
.B u
Undo the last move, if undo is on (\c
.BR \-u ).
.TP
.B n
Start a new game, after asking.
.TP
.B p
Show the save string of the game being played.
.TP
.B c
Color, or black and white.
.TP
.B ?
The keys, on the board; any key goes back.
.TP
.B q
Quit, printing the command that carries on the game.
.SH RESOURCES
Under the program's name, in
.B ~/.Xdefaults
or loaded with
.BR xrdb (1):
.TP
.B x2089.geometry
The window's size and place.
.TP
.B x2089.font
The font for the score and messages.
.TP
.B "x2089.mono: true"
Black and white.
.PP
The options on the command line win over these.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.2089
The best score for each board size, shared with
.BR 2089 (6)
and
.BR xm2089 (6):
one save string a line, the game as it stood at its best.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR 2089 (6),
.BR xm2089 (6),
.BR xrdb (1)
.PP
https://github.com/nfinit/2089
